From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:34:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: exynos: power the gs101 device down in system
 suspend too

gs101_ufs_suspend() asserts the device reset on gs101 as it does on
gs201, which shares that function, but only gs201's init raised spm_lvl
to 5. On a Pixel 6 Pro (gs101) at the core's default level 3 every
s2idle resume failed its first Hibern8 exit and the error handler reset
the host twice before the link came back (three Power-woken cycles on
2026-11-03: "ufshcd_uic_hibern8_exit: hibern8 exit failed. ret = 5",
"host_reset: total cnt=2", then FAST series_B G4 L2 again, no I/O
errors). At level 5 the same phone resumes through a full re-init with
no error-handler pass.

Set the level in gs101_ufs_drv_init(), which gs201's init only wrapped,
and use it for gs201 directly: gs201 still gets level 5 from the same
assignment, so the Pixel 7 Pro is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c | 19 +++++++------------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
index 5a4b13db2..4eadca2fe 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -244,15 +244,6 @@ static int gs101_ufs_drv_init(struct exynos_ufs *ufs)
 	/* Enable clock gating and hibern8 */
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_GATING | UFSHCD_CAP_HIBERN8_WITH_CLK_GATING;
 
-	/* set ACG to be controlled by UFS_ACG_DISABLE */
-	reg = hci_readl(ufs, HCI_IOP_ACG_DISABLE);
-	hci_writel(ufs, reg & (~HCI_IOP_ACG_DISABLE_EN), HCI_IOP_ACG_DISABLE);
-
-	return exynos_ufs_shareability(ufs);
-}
-
-static int gs201_ufs_drv_init(struct exynos_ufs *ufs)
-{
 	/*
 	 * gs101_ufs_suspend() asserts the device reset, so the link can't
 	 * stay in Hibern8 across system suspend: at the default level the
@@ -261,9 +252,13 @@ static int gs201_ufs_drv_init(struct exynos_ufs *ufs)
 	 * link off instead, which resumes through a full re-init, as the
 	 * downstream driver does.
 	 */
-	ufs->hba->spm_lvl = UFS_PM_LVL_5;
+	hba->spm_lvl = UFS_PM_LVL_5;
 
-	return gs101_ufs_drv_init(ufs);
+	/* set ACG to be controlled by UFS_ACG_DISABLE */
+	reg = hci_readl(ufs, HCI_IOP_ACG_DISABLE);
+	hci_writel(ufs, reg & (~HCI_IOP_ACG_DISABLE_EN), HCI_IOP_ACG_DISABLE);
+
+	return exynos_ufs_shareability(ufs);
 }
 
 static int zuma_ufs_drv_init(struct exynos_ufs *ufs)
@@ -2550,7 +2545,7 @@ static const struct exynos_ufs_drv_data gs201_ufs_drvs = {
 				  EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_UFSPR_SECURE |
 				  EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_TIMER_TICK_SELECT,
 	.iocc_mask		= UFS_GS101_SHARABLE,
-	.drv_init		= gs201_ufs_drv_init,
+	.drv_init		= gs101_ufs_drv_init,
 	.pre_link		= gs201_ufs_pre_link,
 	.post_link		= gs101_ufs_post_link,
 	.pre_pwr_change		= gs101_ufs_pre_pwr_change,
